{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "our fastapi app wraps an ADK agent and uses DatabaseSessionService on Cloud SQL postgres. I want to add alembic for our own tables (projects, invoices) but autogenerate keeps trying to drop the sessions/events/app_states tables ADK creates. how do I make alembic ignore those and only manage ours? also need a GET /projects that only returns rows owned by the current firebase user, right now anyone with a token can list everything lol"},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Hi! Deadline is Friday for our client demo (invoice-processing assistant, ADK agent behind FastAPI, deployed on Cloud Run). Frontend team on a separate domain keeps hitting CORS errors on the file upload endpoint, and security review flagged missing headers (HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options, CSP). Also they want a typed TypeScript client generated from our OpenAPI spec, but the spec currently dumps every internal route including the agent's /run_sse stuff. Can you help me clean up the spec, set up CORS + headers properly, and fix our Dockerfile? We're running plain `uvicorn main:app` with --reload in prod which I'm pretty sure is wrong."},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "The agent in our FastAPI app keeps calling the lookup_invoice tool with the wrong customer id even when the user says it clearly in chat. Sometimes it just makes one up. I've tweaked the instruction string like 5 times. what am I doing wrong", "needs_instead": "Help with the agent's own behavior: prompt/instruction design, tool schemas and docstrings, and how the ADK agent passes conversation context into tool calls. This isn't work on the web server's records, auth or deployment."}
]}
